\f0\fs28 \cf2 \cb3 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
This script will check your Yahoo Fantasy Football league to see if any teams have exceeded roster limits. If a team is over the limit the script will send an email to the specified address(es). To send a text message you can setup a Shortcuts automation on an iPhone to pick up the email and send a text message, not sure if there is an equivalent for Android.
\f1\b \
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \cb1 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 First time setup:\

\f0\b0 \cf2 \cb3 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
- Download and install the latest version of Python\
	{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.python.org/downloads/"}}{\fldrslt https://www.python.org/downloads/}}\
	- When prompted during install say yes to allow paths longer that 260 characters\
	- When prompted during install say yes to add commands directory to PATH
\f1\b \

\f0\b0 \cf0 \cb4 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 - On Mac: Navigate to '/Applications/Python 3.13/\'93 and run \'93Install Certificates.command\'94\cb1 \
	- This will install the necessary SSL certificates for sending an email\
- In a cmd window run the following to add required modules for Python\
	\'93py -m pip install requests\'94 (on Mac \'93pip install requests\'94)\
	\'93py -m pip install xmltodict\'94 (on Mac \'93pip install xmltodict\'94)\
	\cb5 \'93py -m pip install pyyaml\'94 (on Mac \'93pip install pyyaml\'94) - NOT SURE IF NEEDED\cb1 \
