\cf0 \cb6 - Steps for downloading package\cb1 \
- Create configuration file\
	- Make a copy of \'93config_template.yaml\'94 called \'93config.yaml\'94\
	- Open \'93config.yaml\'94 and edit as noted in the steps below\
	- Set the \'93current_year\'94 value to the current league year\
	- Set the values under \'93Roster_Limits\'94 in accordance with your league rules \
- You will need to create a Yahoo developer app so the script can access the Yahoo API\
	- In a web browser navigate to: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://developer.yahoo.com/apps/"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 \cb3 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
https://developer.yahoo.com/apps/}}\cf2 \cb3 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\
	- Click the \'93Create an App\'94 button\
		- Application Name: give it any name you like (i.e. FantasyShameBot)\
		- Description: can be left blank\
		- Homepage URL: can be left blank\
		- Redirect URI(s): https://localhost:8080\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 		- Under OAuth Client Type select \'93Confidential Client\'94\
		- Under API Permissions check the box for \'93Fantasy Sports\'94 and select \'93Read\'94 option\
	- Click the \'93Create App\'94 button\
	- Copy the \'93Client ID\'94 value and enter it in \'93config.yaml\'94 as the \'93consumer_key\'94 value\
	- Copy the  \'93Client Secret\'94 value and enter it in \'93config.yaml\'94 as the \'93consumer_secret\'94 value\
- In a web browser navigate to your Yahoo Fantasy Football league\'92s page\
	- Take note of the ID number in the URL for the league page. It will look something like below, the highlighted part is the league ID:\
	https://football.fantasysports.yahoo.com/?lid=\cb7 1231234\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb4 	- Copy this number and enter it in \'93config.yaml\'94 as the \'93league_id\'94 value\cb3 \
- In order to for the script to send an email you will need to create an app password in a google account\
	- I use a secondary account for this as an app password is not recommended due to security risk. This account is simply used as the \'93from\'94 account to give the script access to send an email using google\'92s smtp service.\
	- In a browser navigate to gmail (or google drive, etc.)\
	- Click on your account logo (upper right corner) and select \'93Manage your Google Account\'94\
	- Click on Security on the left side\
	- Under \'93How you sign into Google\'94 click on \'932-Step Verification\'94\
		- Note 2-step verification is required to enable and app password\
	- Scroll to the bottom and look for a section called \'93App passwords\'94\
		- If you see that section click on the right arrow\
		- If you do not see that section go to the address bar and cut off everything from \'93signinoptions\'94 right and replace it will \'93apppasswords\'94\
			- I.e. https://myaccount.google.com/u/0/\cb7 signinoptions/xyz123\cb3 \
			- Change to https://myaccount.google.com/u/0/\cb7 apppasswords\
\cb4 			- The /u/0 may not be there, so the address could simply be https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords\
	- Type in a name for the app password and click \'93Create\'94. This can be anything, it is just for your reference.\
	- Copy the app password that is shown in the pop up window and enter it in \'93config.yaml\'94 as the \'93password\'94 value\
	- In \'93config.yaml\'94 set the \'93senderMail\'94 value as the email address of the account used to create the app password\
	- In \'93config.yaml\'94 set the \'93receiverMail\'94 value as the email address(s) of the account that you want to receive the email notification\
		- Multiple email addresses can be specified by separating them with a comma and space, ie \'93abc@example.com, 123@example.com\'94\cb3 \
- Open the \'93Task Scheduler\'94 application to create a task to run the script\
	- On the right side click on \'93Create Task\'85\'94\
	- Give the task a name, ie \'93ShameBot\'94\
	- Select the option for \'93Run whether user is logged on or not\'94\
	- Select the \'93Triggers\'94 tab then click on \'93New\'85\'94 and set whatever schedule you would like\
	- Select the \'93Actions\'94 tab then click on \'93New\'85\'94\
		- Program/script: Make this the path to python.exe, default is \'93C:\\Users\\<USERNAME>\\AppData\\Local\\Python\\pythoncore-<VERSION>\\python.exe\'94\
		- Add arguments: Make this the path to the ShameBoy.py file, ie \'93C:\\ShameBot\\ShameBot.py\'94\
		- Start in: Make this the path to the ShameBot folder, ie C:\\ShameBot\
	- Click \'93OK\'94 to save the task\
